## Try the repossession workflow

1. Log in as Thanish, tick an item, choose Credit (e.g. 6 instalments), place the order.
2. Log out, log in as the manager, open **Overdue checks**.
3. Run the check with a date about 1 month + 1 day ahead (Pending -> Overdue), then ~8 days after that
   (late fee, Warning 1), then +7 days each run for Warning 2, Warning 3 and finally Repossessed.
4. Check **Reports** (repossessed items, audit log), the **Catalogue** (second-hand item back in stock)
   and log in as Thanish to see warnings and the credit blacklist.

## Where the report's pieces live

| Report item                          | File |
|--------------------------------------|------|
| Enums (Tables 1-5)                   | Domain/Enums.cs |
| IObserver / IPricingStrategy / IPaymentState | Domain/Interfaces.cs |
| User, Staff, Customer                | Domain/Users.cs |
| Furniture, Sofa, Table, Bed, Wardrobe| Domain/Furniture.cs |
| Pricing strategies                   | Domain/Pricing.cs |
| Payment, CashPayment, CreditPayment  | Domain/Payments.cs |
| State pattern classes                | Domain/PaymentStates.cs |
| Order                                | Domain/Order.cs |
| Inventory (Observer subject)         | Domain/Inventory.cs |
| Store (Singleton), save/load JSON    | Domain/Store.cs, Domain/Snapshot.cs |
| Factories                            | Domain/Factories.cs |
| AuditLog (Singleton)                 | Domain/AuditLog.cs |
| Exceptions                           | Domain/Exceptions.cs |
| Website pages                        | Pages/ |
